## Appendix — illustrative filled entry (EXP-010)

> **Example entry — replace or delete.** The numbers below are placeholders to
> show the *format* of a filled entry; they are **not** a measured result.

### EXP-010: smoothing window (example)

**Hypothesis:** A wider smoothing window before differencing denoises the
target derivative and improves test RMSE, up to a point where over-smoothing
removes signal.

**Config diff:** `features.derivatives.smooth_windows: [3, 6, 12]` (superset
materialises all three); arms selected via `features.select.columns`
(`price_diff_1_w3` / `_w6` / `_w12`). One frozen superset, three arms.

**Result:** *(illustrative — not measured)*
`price_diff_1_w3`: test RMSE 0.000 · `_w6`: 0.000 · `_w12`: 0.000.

**Finding:** *(to be filled after the arms are scored with
`make evaluate RUN_ID=`)*

**MLflow runs:** <!-- e.g. abc123 (w3), def456 (w6), ghi789 (w12); tags exp_id=EXP-010, series=B -->

